// Title: Potential Lateral Movement via Windows Remote Shell
// Sigma ID: 79df3f68-dccb-48e9-9171-b75cbc37c51d
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Liran Ravich
// Date: 2025-10-22 | Modified: 2026-11-21
// ATT&CK: lateral-movement, T1021.006
// Description: Detects a child process spawned by 'winrshost.exe', which suggests remote command execution
//   through Windows Remote Shell (WinRs) and may indicate potential lateral movement activity.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use of WinRM within the organization
// References:
//   - https://web.archive.org/web/20260615052554/https://cardinalops.com/blog/living-off-winrm-abusing-complexity-in-remote-management/
//   - https://www.ired.team/offensive-security/lateral-movement/winrs-for-lateral-movement
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/9493cf5c565d7a01b8f064e01a51e1b94057e4bb/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_winrshost_command_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\winrshost.exe" and (not(FolderPath =~ "C:\\Windows\\System32\\conhost.exe"))
